implementation.summary:
Added the opt-in `?indoorLandscapeGate=on` (exact `=on`, default OFF). On an armed indoor frame, the client now skips the landscape when the portal walk reaches no outside portal. Retail does the same: PView::DrawCells (acclient.c:461476) runs LScape::draw (:307754: sky, terrain blocks, weather) and the Clear(4) Z-wipe only when `outside_view.view_count` is non-zero.

cells.js tickPortalSeal is now a thin wrapper around the unchanged seal body. The body records the walk's RAW count (`flat[0]`, taken before clipAperturesForPunch), and a new `tickIndoorLandscapeGate` then decides the skip and passes it to the pipeline through the new additive `setIndoorLandscapeSkip`. tickCellVisibility3D records, only while the flag is on and the split is armed, whether every drawn EnvCell is resident and whether a BFS-only drawn cell in view has an outdoor portal.

The skip is taken only when all of these hold; anything unknown draws the world:
- the raw count is 0, and a second walk through a wider frustum is 0 too;
- the count has been 0 for 2 ticks;
- all drawn cells are resident (pooled cells and `?cellBugParity` count as unknown);
- no in-view BFS-only cell has a doorway;
- the camera is more than 1 m from every outdoor portal near it.

The pipeline honours the skip only when the split is armed and the viewer is indoors. It sets the world pass's layer mask to 0, so the RenderPass still runs and clears colour and depth. It also disables the depth wipe, forces skyBlocked (sky, sky-capture and horizon passes off) and keeps the seal off. The cells pass and the relayered room shell are untouched. With the flag off, every changed line evaluates exactly as before, so the default render path is the same.

