finding.description:
Retail formats both lines client-side from the AttackerNotification/DefenderNotification payload.
Attacker line: "[Critical hit!  ][Sneak Attack! ][Recklessness! ]You <verb> <target> for N point[s] of <type >damage![ Your target's Critical Protection augmentation allows them to avoid your critical hit!]".
Defender line: "[Critical hit! ][Sneak Attack! ][Reckless! ]<attacker> <verbs> your <part> for N point[s] of <type >damage![ Your Critical Protection augmentation allows you to avoid a critical hit!]".
Holtburger's lines differ in five ways:
- they omit the damage-type word ('piercing', 'fire');
- the defender line reads "X bashes you for 18 points of damage to your chest!";
- the defender line reuses the attacker prefixes ('Critical hit!  ' with two spaces, 'Recklessness! ');
