finding.description:
The session dispatcher drops undecodable messages with no trace. A sub-parser that runs short returns None through `?` (every GameEvent arm is `XEventData::unpack(data, offset)?`, and game_message/unpack.rs:129-131 wraps GameEvent the same way). session/messages/mod.rs then discards the whole message, with no log, counter or diag surface. Three other cases are just as invisible:
- a parse that succeeds but leaves bytes unread (`offset < bytes.len()`, i.e. the parser stopped early);
- a parse that drifted into the next field;
- Unknown opcodes, which get only a log::warn.
__diag.wire cannot see any of this because it counts only ClientEvents that were DISPATCHED. ci-smoke S5 already gates zero DAT parse and decode failures but has no wire equivalent. So a protocol regression against live ACE traffic shows up only as a missing UI reaction. WebAC's parsers warn on unread trailing bytes, and its probe harness reports the remaining bytes per parser.

