finding.description:
The first hops of inbound event delivery are guarded: an exhaustive Rust decode match, `gen-client-event-kinds --check` in CI, and all 58 ClientEventKinds referenced by name in JS. The last hop, from ClientEvent to the plugin bus to a UI, has no consumer check. Diffing `events.emit("X")` names against `onBus("X")` and `.on("X")` subscriptions across app/, scene3d/, plugins/ and ui/ finds 8 events no in-tree code consumes:
- `allegianceInfo` (ACE 0x027C AllegianceInfoResponse);
- `uiEvent`, which carries StartBarber 0x0075, ChannelList 0x0148, ChannelIndex 0x0149, UpdateHAR 0x0257 and AvailableHouses 0x0271, where only the 'age' tag reaches chat and the rest go to console.log;
- `chessUpdate`, `inscriptionShown`, `localizationReady`;
- `houseStatusUpdated`, `hoverEntity`, `animationHookDone`, which are deliberate extension points.
Retail does consume the wire ones, so these are silent fidelity gaps nobody tracks. Separately, the wasm GameEvent dispatcher ends in `_ => {}`, so a newly added GameEvent variant compiles with no consumer anywhere. WebAC pins this class with a registration-coverage test. Theirs is a source-grep test grandfathered in their own ratchet, which is why a lint script fits holtburger better.

